# Two separate reasons to have this file, and only the first is about git:
#
#   - Keep local build output, test evidence and editor files out of the repository.
#   - Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
#     directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published
#     folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there, and everything
#     else in this folder - Source/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by construction.

# Build intermediates. Directory.Build.props sends them to .build/ at the repository root, but
# a build run from another directory can still drop them beside the csproj.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Test evidence stays on disk, never in git: reports and captures grow without limit (a Pickle
# run leaves tens of megabytes, a matrix gigabytes). The text summary of each run lives in docs/runs/.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
Tests/Results/
evidence/

# Texture and icon derivatives: DirectDraw Surface files are large and regenerable, and the .ico
# files are local Explorer folder icons made from ModIcon.png and Preview.png.
*.dds
*.ico

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of the
# repository, hundreds of megabytes, and one has already landed inside a mod folder.
.claude/

# Showcase notes: French working notes, deleted once Preview.png and ModIcon.png are done.
PROMPT_*.md

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
